<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia June palm oil output seen down 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Malaysia June palm oil output seen down 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's palm oil output in June was expected to fall by 1.0 percent to 783,000 tonnes from May, crop forecaster Ivan Wong said on Friday.</p>
<p>Wong estimated palm oil stocks at the end of June at 770,000 tonnes, compared with the Palm Oil Registration and Licensing Authority's (PORLA) 711,841 tonnes at end-May.</p>
<p>Palm oil exports in June were expected at 615,000 tonnes against 626,606 tonnes in May, he said.  </p>
<p>In a report, Wong said latest partial data for first-half June showed the performance of major producers/millers ranged from up five percent to down five percent.</p>
<p>On Malaysian palm oil prices, Wong said he expected Friday's closing to provide a better indication of next week's market direction.</p>
<p>At midday Friday, third position September crude palm oil futures contract was up one ringgit at 1,195 ringgit a tonne.  </p>
